-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",354,{
[11297]="7000AB9E\n1\tTalk to Taskmaster Dromdas at Gramsfoot and complete a patrol through the Ettenmoors as a Troll (Cost: 500 Commendations)\tTaskmaster Dromdas is at Gramsfoot. Angmar's army wishes to dislodge the Free Peoples from the Ettenmoors and has enlisted the assistance of trolls to undertake the endeavour. Of course, the work of Angmar must continue and the troll's work must be completed. If you wish to help the trolls, you should speak with Taskmaster Dromdas again.\n2\tTalk to Taskmaster Dromdas at Gramsfoot\tTaskmaster Dromdas is at Gramsfoot. You should return to Taskmaster Dromdas and inform him that you did the work he requested done.\n",
[11298]="7006AD84\n1\tSlay spiders in Tâkhdar (total: 10)\030Collect the trader's misplaced shipment parcels (total: 3)\tSpiders and their captured prey can be found in Shak Phêlex, on the eastern side of Tâkhdar. Slay spiders throughout Tilmakhím and collect Ilzhâna's missing probably-not-contraband parcels. The spiders probably dragged them back to their nest in Shak Phêlex.\n2\tReturn to Ilzhâna\tIlzhâna can be found at Tilmakhím on the western side of Tâkhdar. Return to Ilzhâna with the parcels.\n",
[11299]="700385FF\n1\tTalk to Éowyn and defend Entwade\tÉowyn can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras. Éowyn has asked you to ride with her to Entwade to combat the White Hand forces. You should speak to her when you are ready.\n2\tTalk to Éowyn outside Meduseld\tÉowyn can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras. You have bested the White Hand at Entwade and returned to Edoras. You should speak to Éowyn.\n",
[11300]="7003EBE4\n1\tDefeat sickle-flies upon the High Moor (total: 6)\tSickle-flies infest the High Moor in the Trollshaws. Canaddal has asked you to purge the High Moor of sickle-flies.\n2\tTalk to Canaddal\tCanaddal is encamped on the High Moor in the Trollshaws. You should return to Canaddal and let him know that you have done as he asked.\n",
[11301]="7000C385\n1\tBring the sharpened post to Aeglas in his cell in the Goblin-town prison\030Collect a sharp post from the tunnels above the Goblin-town prison\tStacks of bound posts lie in the main tunnels of Goblin-town. Aeglas believes that he can turn the Orcs and goblins against one another, but his plan requires that you collect a sharp post for him.\n",
[11302]="7002F430\n1\tFind the entrance to the drake's lair\tThe drake's lair is likely somewhere along the cliffs north of Eaworth. You should hunt for the drake's lair.\n2\tTalk to the treasure hunters in the Wyrmdelf\tThe Wyrmdelf lies to the north-east of Eaworth. You should explore the Wyrmdelf.\n3\tDefeat creatures within the Wyrmdelf (total: 15)\tThe treasure-hunters believe the Wyrmdelf to be the lair of a dragon, not understanding that drakes do not hoard wealth as dragons do. You should defeat as many creatures within the Wyrmdelf as you can.\n4\tFind passage to Fang Tor\tFrom the outside, you could see a high ledge, Fang Tor, that might be accessible from the Wyrmdelf. You should find the passage out onto Fang Tor.\n",
[11303]="70008B0F\n1\tTalk to Elrond\tLord Elrond is in the library of his house in Rivendell. Anornaneth has asked you to bring word of her fears concerning Helegrod to Elrond.\n",
[11304]="700372D9\n1\tCollect aurochs meat (total: 6)\030Collect deer meat (total: 6)\030Collect hides (total: 10)\030Collect ivory (total: 6)\030Defeat wolves in the Broadacres (total: 8)\tMeat and ivory can be collected from the aurochs to the south and west and the deer to the north, south, and east. Hides can be collected from wolves, deer, and aurochs. Baldmund has asked you to help provision the town for the coming siege.\n2\tDeliver provisions to the provision stockpile\tThe provision stores are in Stoke, outside the inn. You should bring the provisions you gathered to the provision stockpile.\n3\tTalk to Baldmund\tBaldmund is at the inn in Stoke. You should return to Baldmund and let him know that you have done as he requested.\n",
[11305]="70007F1D\n1\tBring the aurochs-meat to Bogi\030Collect aurochs-meat (total: 4)\tHerds of aurochs are found throughout the hills to the west of Frerin's Court. Kill some of the beasts and bring their meat back to Bogi.\n",
[11306]="7001078B\n1\tFind the best place to catch amberjacks\tThe fish that best represent the dwarves can be found inside of Thorin's Hall. You should go to Thorin's Hall and collect fish for the Lithe Festival.\n2\tCollect amberjacks from Thorin's Hall (total: 3)\tThe fish that best represent the dwarves can be found inside of Thorin's Hall. You should go to Thorin's Hall and collect fish for the Lithe Festival.\n3\tFind the best place in Celondim to catch luillim\tThe fish that best represent those loved by the Elves can be found by fishing along the docks of Celondim, in Ered Luin. You should gather fish from Celondim to help supply the Lithe Festival in the Shire.\n4\tCollect luillim from Celondim (total: 3)\tThe fish that best represent those loved by the Elves can be found by fishing along the docks of Celondim, in Ered Luin. You should gather fish from Celondim to help supply the Lithe Festival in the Shire.\n5\tLook for the best place to catch drum\tThe fish that best represent those loved by Men can be found by fishing at the Pond, near Pierson's farm to the south of Bree-town. You should gather fish from Bree to help supply the Lithe Festival in the Shire.\n6\tCollect drum from the pond (total: 3)\tThe fish that best represent those loved by Men can be found by fishing at the Pond, near Pierson's farm to the south of Bree-town. You should gather fish from Bree to help supply the Lithe Festival in the Shire.\n7\tTalk to Neddie Grubb in Bywater\tNeddie Grubb awaits your diverse collection of fish in Bywater, in the Shire. You should bring the fish to Neddie Grubb so that the pond can be properly stocked for the Lithe Festival.\n8\tTalk to Neddie Grubb in Bywater\tNeddie Grubb awaits your diverse collection of fish in Bywater, in the Shire. You should bring the fish to Neddie Grubb so that Bywater can be properly stocked for the Lithe Festival.\n",
[11307]="7001BE5A\n1\tTalk to Refr Quicksilver\tSeek out dwarves near a cave in the central Lone-lands near the ruins inhabited by Dourhands. Hunulf mentioned that there have been a fair number of dwarves passing through the Lone-lands as of late.\n",
[11308]="7004E924\n1\tCollect tarnished gems\tCollect tarnished gems.\n2\tCollect tarnished gems (total: 10)\tYou should collect tarnished gems from the Orc-kind in Glimmerdeep mine.\n3\tBring the gems to Agátur\tYou should bring the gems to Agátur in Skarháld.\n",
[11309]="7002720D\n1\tFind the owner of the stolen keepsake\tThe remnant of the Boar-clan dwells in Lower Barnavon. You should find the owner of the medallion you found.\n",
[11310]="7006B602\n1\tDefeat bandits and recover sacks of rice (total: 8)\tThe bandits that stole the farmers rice can be found north of Ekagar in Ambarûl.\n2\tBring the sacks of rice to Turizi\tYou have recovered the stolen rice. You should return to Turizi at Ekagar in Ambarûl.\n",
[11311]="7006AA95\n1\tSearch the bandit camp for the Ghôlkhas patriarch's armour\tBandits tend to lurk in north-west Tâkhdar. Okhtâr Ghôlkhas, head of a prominent family, has asked you to retrieve heirloom armour a group of bandits called the Denjâri stole from the family tomb. He has asked you to retrieve it.\n2\tDefeat Denjâri bandits (total: 8)\tDefeat Denjâri bandits.\n3\tSearch for clues as to the armour's whereabouts\t\n4\tLook for Rashâm in the black market of Kheb Hanût\tRashâm can be found in the black market of Kheb Hanût. A letter from the Denjâri bandits' leader says she has sold the Ghôlkhas's stolen armour to a black market fence named Rashâm.\n5\tSpeak with Rashâm in Kheb Hanût\tSpeak with Rashâm in Kheb Hanût.\n",
[11312]="7000188A\n1\tCollect stolen yeast (total: 3)\tSacks of yeast can be found around the camps at Thurûm, north of Othrikar. You should collect sacks of yeast stolen from Othrikar.\n2\tBring the yeast to Hornbori\tHornbori is at Othrikar. You should bring the stolen yeast to Hornbori.\n",
[11313]="700076CC\n1\tReturn the notes to Oddvarr\030Recover Oddvarr's notes (quantity: see journal)\tTarkrîp Orcs from around Cirith Nûr, west to north-west of Oddvarr in the North Bree-fields, have stolen Oddvarr's precious notes. Oddvarr can be found south-east of Hengstacer Farm near the ruins. Oddvarr's notes are missing, and he suspects the Tarkrîp Orcs ran off with them. One of the Orcs must have them, if you can only find which one.\n",
[11314]="70007807\n1\tCollect the stolen pipe-weed\tHimloc's stolen pipe-weed should be in the brigand-occupied ruins of Ost Baranor, south and slightly to the west of Constable Bolger's house. Constable Bolger has asked you to recover Himloc's pipe-weed from the brigands.\n2\tBring the stolen pipe-weed to Himloc Grouse in Staddle\tHimloc Grouse is in the town square of Staddle. You recovered Himloc's pipe-weed from the Blackwold brigands, as Constable Bolger asked of you. You should return it to Himloc as soon as possible.\n",
[11315]="7002BF8A\n1\tCollect relics of the Rohirrim (total: 10)\tRelics of the Rohirrim can be found throughout the camp and on the treasure-seekers at Atburg, south-east of Aculf's camp in the Rushgore. Aculf has asked you to recover relics of the Rohirrim from the brigand treasure-seekers.\n2\tBring the relics you recovered to Eowils outside Atburg in the Rushgore\tEowils is outside Atburg in the Rushgore, south-east of Aculf's camp. Aculf told you to report your successes to the scout Eowils.\n",
[11316]="7002BF99\n1\tTalk to someone at Aculf's camp in the Rushgore\tThere are Rohirrim at Aculf's camp in the Rushgore, north-west of Atburg. You should bring the Dunlending relic to one of the Rohirrim.\n2\tCollect relics of the Dunlendings (total: 5)\tDunlending relics might be found on brigands at Atburg, south-east of Aculf's camp in the Rushgore. Bagmund wants you to find more Dunlending relics for him.\n3\tBring the Dunlending relics to Bagmund at Aculf's camp in the Rushgore\tBagmund is at Aculf's camp in the Rushgore, north-west of Atburg. You should bring the Dunlending relics to Bagmund at once.\n",
[11317]="7002BF98\n1\tTalk to someone at Aculf's camp in the Rushgore\tThere are Rohirrim at Aculf's camp in the Rushgore, north-west of Atburg. You should bring this relic to one of the Rohirrim.\n2\tCollect relics of the Easterlings (total: 5)\tEasterling relics may be found on brigands at Atburg, south-east of Aculf's camp in the Rushgore. Wynstan bade you find more of the Easterling relics.\n3\tBring the Easterling relics to Wynstan at Aculf's camp in the Rushgore\tWynstan is at Aculf's camp in the Rushgore, north-west of Atburg. You should bring the Easterling relics to Wynstan at once.\n",
[11318]="70002CD1\n1\tBring the aurochs-skull back to Santtu at Lehmä-koti\030Collect Aurochs Skull (quantity: see journal)\tThe aurochs skulls are likely in Skathmur in the eastern part of Ram Dúath. Santtu has asked you to recover a stolen aurochs skull.\n",
[11319]="70028AD1\n1\tCollect stacks of stolen lumber (total: 12)\tStolen stacks of wood can be found around the Galtrev Lumber-camp, just north of Galtrev. You should gather wood as you investigate the Dragon-clan thieves in the Galtrev Lumber-camp.\n2\tBring the recovered wood-stacks to Fraid\tFraid can be found at the broken waggon near the Galtrev Lumber-camp in Pren Gwydh. You should bring the wood you recovered from the Galtrev Lumber-camp to Fraid.\n",
[11320]="70048C68\n1\tFind first clue\030Find second clue\030Find third clue\030Find fourth clue\tA thief stole supplies from the Agarnaith Ranger camp and fled into the swamp. You should follow the thief's trail.\n2\tConfront the thief\tThe trail has led you to a young goblin standing by the path. You should confront the thief.\n3\tFind the thief\tThe goblin thief has run east, deeper into the swamp. You should chase after the thief!\n4\tDefeat infected ambushers (total: 3)\tWhile chasing the goblin thief, you were ambushed by crazed Orcs. You should defeat your ambushers!\n5\tFind Viznak's hideout\tThe goblin has been carried off, but Rhadrog seems to have found his hideout nearby. You should find Viznak's hideout.\n6\tTalk to Faeron\tFaeron can be found at Viznak's hideout. You should talk to Faeron.\n",
[11321]="70050A06\n1\tRecover hot cross buns\030Recover plum pudding\030Recover gingerbread\030Recover peppermint treats\030Recover a flask of wassail\030Recover fruit cake\tYou should recover the sweets.\n2\tReturn to Winter-home\tYou should return to the Festival Announcer in Frostbluff with the treats.\n3\tYou should deliver the sweets to the children of Winter-home.\t\n4\tTalk to the child\tOne of the children in Winter-home wishes to talk with you.\n",
[11322]="700079D1\n1\tBring the satchel to Ann Granger\030Collect Ann Granger's satchel\tBlackwolds' Roost lies in the ruins south of the Hunter's Lodge. Ann Granger has asked you to go to Blackwolds' Roost and recover her stolen satchel.\n",
[11323]="7003A694\n1\tCollect enemy tools (0/8)\tThere are tools cast aside or laying about Mate Isernore.\n2\tCollect enemy tools (total: 8)\tThere are tools cast aside or laying about Mate Isernore. You should collect any tools you find and bring them to the overseer of Wid Isernore where they will be put to good use.\n3\tYou should bring the tools you gathered to the mine-overseer in Wid Isernore.\t\n",
[11324]="70017531\n1\tBring the innards to Pentlenn at the Shadowed Refuge\030Collect handfuls of grodbog-innards (total: 12)\tSkûmfil is south-east of the Shadowed Refuge. Pentlenn would like to study the innards of the gredbyg at Skûmfil to see if there is any disease within them that could be affecting the Orcs.\n",
[11325]="70020B46\n1\tGet the shrew-stomping boots from the nearby crate\tThe boots needed for stomping on shrews can be found near the stairs of the Festival Garden. You should collect the boots from the crate and drag them to your skill bar, for they will be needed to deter shrews.\n2\tEnter the garden space\tThe pesky shrews can be found in the garden's centre in Duillond's Festival Garden, and the shrew-stomping boots are in your inventory. You should locate the boots in your inventory and slot them as a skill. These boots can be used to stomp on obnoxious shrews infesting the garden. When you have done so, wait in the centre of the garden, for Dinedhrín has challenged you to defeat the large and ornery shrew that appears during every shrew-whacking game. NOTE: To slot the boots as a skill, drag the 'Enormous Boots' item from your inventory to your skill bar. Pesky shrews are immune to all other attacks and offensive manoeuvres.\n3\tSlot the shrew-stomping boots in your skill bar and wait for the onslaught\tThe enormous shrew can be found in the centre space of Duillond's Festival Garden. Dinedhrín has asked you to defeat the enormous shrew, who only appears once per round. NOTE: To slot the boots as a skill, drag the 'Enormous Boots' item from your inventory to your skill bar. Pesky shrews are immune to all other attacks and offensive manoeuvres.\n4\tBe the first to stomp the enormous shrew\tThe enormous shrew can be found in the centre space of Duillond's Festival Garden. Dinedhrín has asked you to defeat the enormous shrew, who only appears once per round. NOTE: To slot the boots as a skill, drag the 'Enormous Boots' item from your inventory to your skill bar. Pesky shrews are immune to all other attacks and offensive manoeuvres. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tTalk to Dinedhrín\tDinedhrín stands in the Elven Garden at Duillond. You should speak with Dinedhrín of your victory against the shrews.\n",
[11326]="70020B49\n1\tGet the shrew-stomping boots from the nearby crate\tThe boots needed for stomping on shrews can be found near the stairs of the Festival Garden. You should collect the boots from the crate and drag them to your skill bar, for they will be needed to deter shrews.\n2\tDrag your boots to your skill bar and enter the garden\tPesky shrews can be found in the centre space of Duillond's Festival Garden. The pesky shrews can be found in the garden's centre in Duillond's Festival Garden, and the shrew-stomping boots are in your inventory. You should locate the boots in your inventory and slot them as a skill. These boots can be used to stomp on obnoxious shrews infesting the garden. Maengamiel has asked you to defeat many shrews in the garden. NOTE: To slot the boots as a skill, drag the 'Boots of Quite-imaginable Power' item from your inventory to your skill bar. Pesky shrews are immune to all other attacks and offensive manoeuvres.\n3\tSlot the shrew-stomping boots in your skill bar and wait for the onslaught\tPesky shrews can be found in the centre space of Duillond's Festival Garden. Maengamiel has asked you to defeat many shrews at your leisure. NOTE: To slot the boots as a skill, drag the 'Boots of Quite-imaginable Power' item from your inventory to your skill bar. Pesky shrews are immune to all other attacks and offensive manoeuvres.\n4\tDrive away pesky shrews (total: 10)\tPesky shrews can be found in the centre space of Duillond's Festival Garden. Maengamiel has asked you to defeat many shrews at your leisure. NOTE: To slot the boots as a skill, drag the 'Boots of Quite-imaginable Power' item from your inventory to your skill bar. Pesky shrews are immune to all other attacks and offensive manoeuvres.\n5\tTalk to Maengamiel\tMaengamiel stands in the Elven Garden at Duillond. You should speak with Maengamiel of your victory against the shrews.\n",
[11327]="70020B48\n1\tGet the shrew-stomping boots from the nearby crate\tThe boots needed for stomping on shrews can be found near the stairs of the Festival Garden. You should collect the boots from the crate and drag them to your skill bar, for they will be needed to deter shrews.\n2\tYou have been given boots for stomping on shrews; you should slot these as a skill and enter the garden\tPesky shrews can be found in the centre space of Duillond's Festival Garden. You should locate the boots in your inventory and slot them as a skill. These boots can be used to stomp on obnoxious shrews infesting the garden. When you have done so, you should wait in the centre of the garden for the shrews to appear. Brangloth has insisted that you defeat many shrews before the game event comes to an end. NOTE: To slot the boots as a skill, drag the 'Boots of Quite-imaginable Power' item from your inventory to your skill bar. Pesky shrews are immune to all other attacks and offensive manoeuvres.\n3\tSlot the shrew-stomping boots in your skill bar and wait for the onslaught\tPesky shrews can be found in the centre space of Duillond's Festival Garden. Brangloth has insisted that you defeat many shrews before the game event comes to an end. NOTE: To slot the boots as a skill, drag the 'Boots of Quite-imaginable Power' item from your inventory to your skill bar. Pesky shrews are immune to all other attacks and offensive manoeuvres.\n4\tDrive away pesky shrews (total: 10)\tPesky shrews can be found in the centre space of Duillond's Festival Garden. Brangloth has insisted that you defeat many shrews before the game event comes to an end. NOTE: To slot the boots as a skill, drag the 'Boots of Quite-imaginable Power' item from your inventory to your skill bar. Pesky shrews are immune to all other attacks and offensive manoeuvres. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tTalk to Brangloth\tBrangloth awaits you in the Festival Garden of Duillond. You should speak with Brangloth of your success against the pesky shrews.\n",
[11328]="7006C091\n1\tCollect samples of harathar (total: 4)\tThe harathar samples can be found in the TBD of TBD. A mason named TBD would like to get a closer look at some harathar outcroppings. He has asked you to collect some samples for him.\n2\tTBD Ziggurat Mason can be found TBD Location. You have acquired several good samples of harathar. It is time to return to TBD Ziggurat Mason for him to inspect the goods.\t\n",
})
